{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-1835","published":"2026-04-11T11:10:51Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:19:45.889766152Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-33750"],"summary":"nodejs-brace-expansion security update","details":"Brace expansion as known from sh/bash\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nThe brace-expansion library generates arbitrary strings containing a common prefix and suffix. Prior to versions 5.0.5, 3.0.2, 2.0.3, and 1.1.13, a brace pattern with a zero step value (e.g., `{1..2..0}`) causes the sequence generation loop to run indefinitely, making the process hang for seconds and allocate heaps of memory. Versions 5.0.5, 3.0.2, 2.0.3, and 1.1.13 fix the issue. As a workaround, sanitize strings passed to `expand()` to ensure a step value of `0` is not used.(CVE-2026-33750)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nodejs-brace-expansion","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/nodejs-brace-expansion&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.1.11-3.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"noarch":["nodejs-brace-expansion-1.1.11-3.oe2003sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["nodejs-brace-expansion-1.1.11-3.oe2003sp4.src.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-1835.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs-brace-expansion","ecosystem":"openEuler:22.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/nodejs-brace-expansion&distro=openEuler-22.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.1.11-3.oe2203sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"noarch":["nodejs-brace-expansion-1.1.11-3.oe2203sp4.noarch.rpm"],"src":["nodejs-brace-expansion-1.1.11-3.oe2203sp4.src.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-1835.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs-brace-expansion","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/nodejs-brace-expansion&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events"